-- Английска версия на основните страници (само там, където още няма английски текст).
UPDATE site_pages SET title_en = 'History', body_en = 'In the late 19th century, the people of the village of Kurt Dere (today Valchi Dol) sent their children to study in the nearby villages of Karaagach (Brestak) and Kozludzha (Suvorovo). The need for a school of their own kept growing, and in 1880 a school was opened in Valchi Dol. It was housed in the mosque that stood next to today''s fountain in the town square.

The first teacher, Atanas Doychev Yurukchiev, was born on 22 March 1859 in the village of Krivnya near Provadia. He taught all four grades in a single room of the mosque. The school soon became too small for all the children, and in 1902 the construction of a new building began on a sunny meadow with a spring. It was built with money collected by the villagers. At first there were only two classrooms for the first graders. Before the First World War two more classrooms were added, and the building took the shape of the letter "П". Construction continued in 1919 with a second floor, which made it possible to open a lower secondary school (progymnasium) in February 1921.

## After 1944

After 9 September 1944 two more classrooms were built on the upper floor. In 1944 the opening of a high school in Valchi Dol was announced, and regular classes started on 16 January 1945. Students from the high schools in Varna and Provadia were transferred to Valchi Dol; 400 students were enrolled in eight classes. In the summer of the same year the 11th grade was opened, and the high school became complete.

In 1951 the primary school "Vasil Levski" and the high school "Sabi Dichev" were merged into one school. In 1959 the building was extended again with two classrooms and a metalworking workshop, and vocational subjects were introduced: agriculture, crop and livestock farming, farm machinery and soda production, with practical training at the soda plant in Devnya.

In 1968 a vocational secondary school for the chemical industry opened in the same building, to train specialists for the growing chemical industry in the Devnya valley. Because of the growing number of students, four more classrooms were added in the west wing in 1970/71. From 1973/74 the school prepared to become a unified secondary polytechnic school, and for many years students from 1st to 11th grade studied here.

## Today

The present school building, built in 1987, has 22 classrooms, a canteen, an assembly hall, two gyms, metalworking and woodworking workshops, and a floodlit sports ground in the schoolyard. For many years the school in Valchi Dol has been an example for the schools in the region. Today it is a place of learning that the people of the town hold dear, where the present generation of teachers continues the work of their predecessors.' WHERE slug = 'istoriya' AND (title_en IS NULL OR title_en = '');
UPDATE site_pages SET title_en = 'Patron and symbols', body_en = '## Our patron: Vasil Levski

The school is named after Vasil Levski (1837–1873), the leader of the Bulgarian struggle for liberation from Ottoman rule and one of the most respected figures in Bulgarian history.

Vasil Ivanov Kunchev was born in Karlovo. He became known as Levski ("lion-like"), a nickname he probably received in Belgrade at the time of the First Bulgarian Legion for his skill in military training and his courage in the battle with the Turkish garrison on 3 June 1862.

In his letters and in the archive of the revolutionary committees, Levski is known by many other names, among them the Deacon, Aslan Dervishoglu and Dragoycho. From his time as a member of a rebel band he left a short, unfinished autobiography in verse, probably written in 1867–1868.

## School song

The school has its own song, "Song of Vasil Levski School, Valchi Dol". Lyrics by Zheko Zhekov, music by Dyanka Yanakieva. The chorus calls the school "a hundred-year-old hearth of work and dreams" and "youth and a path into life".' WHERE slug = 'patron-i-simvoli' AND (title_en IS NULL OR title_en = '');
UPDATE site_pages SET title_en = 'Mission and goals', body_en = '## Mission

The mission of Vasil Levski School is to support students in their growth and development in a good school environment, with qualified teachers and in partnership with parents and institutions. We want our students to gain not only basic education, but also up-to-date knowledge, skills and competences that they need to succeed in society, with respect for the rights of others and responsible behaviour.

## Strategic goals

- Continuously improving students'' knowledge and skills in general, technical and specialised subjects and in practical training.
- Building patterns of behaviour based on mutual respect for dignity, tolerance, national identity and respect for the rights of everyone.
- Creating opportunities for teachers to improve their qualifications.
- Taking part in municipal and national programmes and in European Union projects, and putting them into practice.' WHERE slug = 'misiya-i-tseli' AND (title_en IS NULL OR title_en = '');
UPDATE site_pages SET title_en = 'Vision', body_en = '"The personality of the learning child is our future, and it needs the teacher''s effort to understand it." – M. Heidegger

The 140-year history of Vasil Levski School has rightly earned it the reputation of the best school in the municipality of Valchi Dol. It is a centre of culture, creativity and learning for young and old. As the central school of the municipality, it will continue to focus on high-quality learning and on developing skills and competences.

Vasil Levski School is a school of opportunities, giving knowledge for the future.

Our teachers work to build a learning environment that encourages and supports every individual to receive an education that meets the needs of modern life; a school where teachers keep improving their professional skills, and where students, teachers and parents form a community that shows tolerance, care and respect for human values.

That is why our vision is:

## A school with traditions – a school with a future' WHERE slug = 'viziya' AND (title_en IS NULL OR title_en = '');
UPDATE site_pages SET title_en = 'Admission', body_en = '## Admission to 8th grade, school year 2026/2027

Vocational class "E-commerce", without intensive or extended study of a foreign language.

1 class – 26 students

Admission score is based on:

- twice the points from the National External Assessment in Bulgarian language and literature;
- twice the points from the National External Assessment in mathematics;
- the grade in geography and economics from the basic education certificate, converted into points;
- the grade in mathematics from the basic education certificate, converted into points.

Admission follows the national schedule of the Ministry of Education and Science. Dates for applications and enrolment, forms and earlier years are on the Bulgarian version of this page. For questions, please contact the school office.' WHERE slug = 'priem' AND (title_en IS NULL OR title_en = '');
UPDATE site_pages SET title_en = 'Projects', body_en = 'The school takes part in national programmes and European projects. Current and recent projects include:

- Project under programme BG05SFPR001-1.010 "Prevention of bullying and violence and reducing aggression in schools", funded with 97,000 euro;
- National programme "Support for the personal development of children and students" 2023, module 2 "School without aggression for a safe school environment";
- "Schools for example" programme of the Teach for Bulgaria foundation ("Zaedno v chas");
- Module "Libraries as a learning environment";
- Project "Student internships – 2";
- "Equal access to school education in times of crisis";
- Project "Education for tomorrow";
- Project "Support for inclusive education".' WHERE slug = 'proekti' AND (title_en IS NULL OR title_en = '');
